INSTALLATION:



If you don't want to see dockerhub on site, then you can search available images in docker using commands:

docker search <image-name>
docker search nginx

	---------------> here nginx is also a image, someone might have taken server created nginx and created an image, so world can use it.
Similarly, like in AWS we select, Ubuntu OS during EC2 launch, but somebody created that AMI of ubuntu and so it is available now for world.

If we want to take that image, istall in our system, need to pull

docker pull <image name>
docker pull nginx

you can check images on your system
docker image ls
or
docker images


to pull image

docker pull <image-name>
docker pull nginx



To create container using pulled image: 

docker run <image-id>
OR
docker run <image-name>

docker run nginx



OR

you can check id using
docker images
"copy id from there "
and 
docker run 41f689c20910
-- Here we have not given any name to container, so it will generate random name.

Now container is created, but it is running in FOREGROUND. You won't able to do any other operation.
Once you try, you will exit from current running container, and this container will be stopped.

Ctrl +c = exit from running container
==================================================================

check here containers
(Old commands)
docker ps
it will show nothing as no running container. So to show all containers in whatever state they are, use
docker ps -a


(New Commands - very easy and specific)
docker container ls
docker container ls -a

=========================================================

SO
now to keep container running even in background

docker run -d <image-name>
docker run -d nginx

If you want to give name to container and keep running in background
docker run -d --name  <name_of_container>  <image-name or image-id>
docker run -d --name  mynginx  nginx
OR
docker run -d --name  mynginx 41f689c20910



So new container name will be "mynginx"

