Let's see our normal operation!
Suppose we have html code, then to host it we have to create file inside nginx server --> inside path /usr/share/nginx/html/________
So suppose we want to create hello.html  here.
We have to write code using nano. But in docker, we use containers, and for that when we install nginx in container using pull --> It doesn't pull everything -> it pull necessary environment or basic OS only -- > and basic command(e.g. touch)

To use extra package, you have to install.
So nano directly won't work.
First tell docker to install nano package. Then write hello.html code file.
 






then 
nano hello.html



To check 

curl localhost/hello.html



So if curl shows you a code, it means you are looking at the HTTP response status from the server.


